According to DEC's "25 Year Product Genealogy", the timeline for the 
machines in question are as follows:

System		Introduction	End of Life
------		------------	-----------
PDP-7		1964 Q2		1969 Q2
PDP-9		1966 Q4		1971 Q3
KA-10		1967		1976 Q1
PDP-9/L		1970 Q2		1971 Q3
PDP-15		1970 Q3		1977
1971		KI-10		1976 Q3
1974		KL-10		1983 Q2
PDP-15/76	1975		1978 Q1
PDP-15 XVM	1976 Q2		1977 Q3

I'm a bit skeptical about this; I'm pretty sure that first customer ship 
of the KL was in 1975.  And of course we can dispute as to exactly when 
the end of life of the KL was... :-)

It is pretty clear that the PDP-15 was quite abruptly terminated; note in 
particular the extremely short product life of XVM.  I heard rumors about 
what happened to the PDP-15 development group (the "Tiger Team"); 
apparently it was as ugly as what happened to the PDP-10 people 6 years 
later but only a relatively small number of people noticed at the time. 
I don't think that I ever even saw a PDP-15 until after it had been 
cancelled.

-- Mark --

