Sure.  But I don't remember a whole system setup.
You may have started working after the last happened.

A customer's system was setup on the east side of MR1-3
almost inch to inch of the floor plan of the customer's
machine room.  After the hardware was set up and checked
out so that all juices were running fine, the software
got installed.  Then there were a suite of test runs
that were done to ensure our standards of executions didn't
have a problem.  Then the system was shut off, very carefully
dismantled and packaged, moved to the loading dock, put on a
truck (including the hoomans ;-)), driven to the customer site,
bay doors opened, and the hoomans took off and started
dis-dismantling the system.

I don't remember a complete system that was set up after 86,
maybe even earlier.


