I'm trying to bring up a VAX 6000/600 I picked up on eBay, and I'm 
seeing the following problem.  When I power up the machine, the fan 
comes on and the panel lights come on for a few seconds; then the lights 
go off, but the fans stay on.  "The lights" includes green lights on the 
four memory boards, but no lights on the CPUs; there is also a red light 
on the DWMBB that goes out when everything else does.  The display on 
the H7206-B shows green for the +14v, but also displays L8: "XMI-1 
module in XMI-2 card cage".

Details: there are six processors, four memory boards, a DEMNA, CIXCD 
and DWMBB/A in the XMI enclosure.  There's a companion DWMBB/B in the BI 
cage (only one is hooked up).  I've wired a three-phase receptacle into 
my single-phase 220v, per guidance posted by Gunther Schadow (thanks!).

Steps: I've reseated everything, of course.  I've tried removing the 
DWMBB/A (unfortunately I don't have another to swap in).  I've removed 
everything except for one proc and one memory card and started the 
machine (yes, I put the proc and memory card in consecutive slots, 
starting from the right).  Nothing changes this behavior.  Pressing the 
reset button on the H7206 causes the lights to come back on for a few 
seconds, then they disappear again and the error indicator shows.  The 
fans spin happily through all of this.

I've dug through the 6000 Platform Technical Manual, the XMI update 
docs, and pretty much everything I can think of to determine what's 
going on.  My question is: does this sound familiar to anyone?  Does 
anyone know what this error *really* means?  What is it measuring? 
Perchance, does anyone have schematics of the H7206-B logic?  Thanks in 
advance for any help you can provide.  -- Ian
