I've exchanged email with Bob, because my ISP has terrible netnews 
connectivity.  <sigh>  However, to share my pain, er learnings with the 
rest of the community....

I've done some troubleshooting on this box, including pretending I'm a 
DEC field engineer and replacing pieces wholesale.  :-)  What I think 
I'm looking at is as follows.

I have checked the interlocks, the temp sensor and the airflow sensor, 
and found nothing amiss.  However, when I got down to the inhibit lines 
coming up from the H7206 (based on some information provided by Bob - 
thanks!), I found 'asserted' lines on the H7214 and H7215 on the XMI 
side (the BI side seems to be fine).  This suggests that the H7206B 
thinks there's something wrong with the XMI bus.

A note on one of the many pieces of information I've read suggested that 
the H7206B wants to know if a particular pad on the XMI bus is 'closed', 
