In article <1143059199.662577.290390@i40g2000cwc.googlegroups.com>, "Bob Armstrong" <bob@jfcl.com> writes:
:  Is there any way to install all these diagnostics on a RD5x drive?

  That depends on how the ELN image was built -- if it has the drivers
  for it, then you can download ELN images via MOP and via hard disk. 

  At least some of the MDM distros can be downloaded via DECnet MOP
  -- it's been two full eons since I've configured and used that
  approach, however.

  If you disk boot MDM, you'll need to set up the diagnostics in the
  [SYS%.SYSMAINT] directory (or into [SYS%.SYSEXE], depending on the 
  release) and use B/R5:100 (if in SYSMAINT) or B/R5:x0000000 (and
  x is the SYSx root) to load the right image.   Off-hand, I don't
  remember which file is the boot file.  (And it likely also varied
  by the MDM release -- the older releases were pretty limited in
  their configuration options.)

  Folks at the support center should be able to help you with this.


