Terry Collins wrote:
> 
> Can anyone tell me of the Alphaserver 2000 requires both power supplies
> working to run?
> 
> TIA.

The AlphaServer 2000 can handle up to 400 watts DC with a single
power supply or with a dual power supply configured in redundant
mode (jumper J3 installed on the backplane). In full power mode
with 2 supplies, it can handle up to 725 watts.

A single power supply or redundant supply supports:

       One CPU
       Two memory modules
       One diskette drive
       Two removable drives
       Eight 3.5-inch StorageWorks hard disks
       Ten I/O slots

If you have a second CPU, you need 2 supplies in full power mode.

-Tom


